{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And Jacob set up a pillar in the place where He had spoken with him.</b> It repeats a second time, 'in the place where He had spoken with him' — this refers to the One above, and it is the place of Bethel where he set up the pillar. 'And Jacob set up a pillar' means he had already set it up; he did not set it up on his return, for on his going he had set it up at the outset, as stated at the beginning of the parashah of VaYetze. The difference between a pillar (מצבה) and an altar (מזבח) is that the pillar is but a single stone, whereas the altar is many stones; also, the altar is built for the purpose of a sacrifice, while the pillar is not for sacrifice but only for the pouring and libation of oil. And because HaShem, may He be exalted, said to him, 'Your name shall no more be called Jacob,' and it is written, 'and He called his name Israel,' he should have said, 'and Israel set up'; but this indicates that 'your name shall no more be called Jacob' is not a prohibition, but rather that he would sometimes be called Jacob and sometimes Israel, as was explained above. Accordingly, Scripture later in this very parashah calls him by both these names: it mentions him by the name Jacob — 'and Jacob set up' — and it mentions him by the name Israel as well — 'and Israel journeyed.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:48.843425358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}